      "rules": [
        {
          "body": "When a subscription can begin decoding before its listener is removed, bind both its cleanup handle and permission to publish a decoded value to the panel visit that started it. Install a provisional cleanup handle before startup; if synchronous publication hides or switches the panel, do not let the outer startup replace the newer visit’s handle. Listener removal stops new reception but does not itself decide whether an already-started decode may publish: after a switch, hide, or synchronous reentry retires the originating visit, its settlement must not update the panel. Preserve bootstrap and later updates for the current visit, including a later visit using the same channel. Verify synchronous bootstrap reentry plus delayed decode across close, switch, and same-channel reopening: retired visits produce no publication and the active visit still receives its bootstrap and later update.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R01"
        }
