      "rules": [
        {
          "body": "Confirm whether subscription startup can emit synchronously and whether the consumer must receive that emission. Identify the consumer lifetime that owns delivery and cleanup, including synchronous callback reentry. Distinguish listener removal from completion of work already started. Confirm whether a transport can be reused across separate visits before using transport identity as a validity check.",
          "category": "applicability",
          "id": "R01"
        },
        {
          "body": "For a consumer that requires bootstrap state, register reception before invoking startup that can emit synchronously. src/channel.js emits bootstrap inline unless deferred, while src/subscription.js originally connects before registering. Check both bootstrap modes and later updates.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R02"
        },
        {
          "body": "Bind permission to publish decoded values to the visit that received the frame. src/subscription.js permits Promise decoding and explicitly states that listener removal does not stop an existing decode. On close or replacement, retire that visit and check its permission immediately before publication. Check pending completion after close and switch while preserving active-visit delivery.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R03"
        },
        {
          "body": "Establish retirement and cleanup ownership before startup can publish. src/workspace-navigation.js explicitly permits publication to synchronously switch or hide the panel. An older startup returning afterward must not overwrite the resulting visit's cleanup ownership. Check inline switch and hide, subsequent updates, and eventual cleanup.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R04"
        },
        {
          "body": "Give each opening an independent lifetime even when it reuses the same transport. src/workspace-navigation.js explicitly supports transport reuse. Check that pending results from a retired opening remain suppressed while the later opening receives bootstrap and updates.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R05"
        },
        {
          "body": "Scope the ordering repair to the presence subscription. The task forbids changing the metrics consumer, and src/metrics-consumer.js deliberately relies on attaching after synchronous bootstrap to count deltas only. Check that presence gains bootstrap delivery while metrics retain their existing output.",
          "category": "preservation",
